% nusselt_dittus_boelter — the Nusselt number of turbulent flow in a smooth tube (simple, for first sizing)
%
% Usage:      Nu = nusselt_dittus_boelter(Re, Pr, heating)
%             heating is true when the fluid is being heated (the wall is hotter than the fluid), false when it is being cooled.
% Computes:   Nu = 0.023 Re^0.8 Pr^n, n = 0.4 for heating and 0.3 for cooling.
% Method:     the Dittus-Boelter correlation.
% Units:      none (all dimensionless).
% Limits:     Re >= 10 000, 0.6 <= Pr <= 160, tube length at least 10 diameters; moderate temperature differences. Outside these
%             the function stops with an error: use nusselt_gnielinski, which is better over a wider range.
% References: Dittus and Boelter, Univ. Calif. Pub. Eng. 2 (1930) 443; Incropera et al., 7th ed., eq. 8.60.
% Check:      Re 50 000, Pr 5, heating: Nu = 0.023 * 50 000^0.8 * 5^0.4 = 251.5 (tools/field-test/eng.mjs).
function Nu = nusselt_dittus_boelter(Re, Pr, heating)
if nargin < 3
  heating = true;
end
if Re < 1e4 || Pr < 0.6 || Pr > 160
  error('nusselt_dittus_boelter: only for Re of at least 10 000 and Pr from 0.6 to 160 (use nusselt_gnielinski)');
end
if heating
  n = 0.4;
else
  n = 0.3;
end
Nu = 0.023 * Re ^ 0.8 * Pr ^ n;
end
